# `ui.pane_rail = off` paints no rail at all.
#
# Three settings: `all` (the default — every pane), `sessions` (the
# older look, where only an AI session pane wore one) and `off`. With
# `off` the first column of a terminal pane is the child's own grid
# again, and no cell of it is the rail's ▌.
command view.toggle_tree
ex set ui.pane_rail=off
ex term printf LL; sleep 30
expect screen contains "LL"
expect screen lacks "▌LL"
expect color 0 2 fg not #98c379

# Back to `all` and the rail is there again.
ex set ui.pane_rail=all
expect color 0 2 fg #98c379
